**State** is data that can change. When it changes, React redraws the component:

```
import { useState } from "react";

export default function App() {
  const [mana, setMana] = useState(0);   // value + setter
  return (
    <button onClick={() => setMana(mana + 1)}>
      Mana: {mana}
    </button>
  );
}
```

Never change state directly (`mana++` does nothing on screen). Always call the **setter**.

A **union type** lists the only values allowed:

```
type Direction = "up" | "down" | "left" | "right";
const path: Direction[] = ["right", "down"];
```

`Direction[]` means "an array of Directions". Now a typo like `"rigth"` is caught by the Runesmith before your hero takes a single step.

